      "body": "# [AMD] Limit AITER DSA decode metadata to the active batch\n\n## Motivation\n\nThe AITER DSA backend preallocates `kv_indptr` for the maximum request-pool\ncapacity and reuses that buffer for smaller decode batches. The AITER metadata\nbuilder consumes the logical length of the tensor it receives. Passing the\ncapacity-sized tensor exposes entries beyond the active batch and can construct\ninvalid persistent MLA work metadata.\n\nOn MI355X TP4 with an FP8 KV cache, the invalid metadata caused eager and CUDA\ngraph execution to fault in:\n\n`aiter::mla_a16w8_qh16_m16x4_n16x1_coex0_mask1_ps`\n\n## Modifications\n\nPass only the active `bs + 1` entries to the AITER metadata builder:\n\n```python\nkv_indptr = kv_indptr[: bs + 1]\n```\n\nThe backing buffer remains preallocated and reused. This change only corrects\nthe logical range passed to `get_mla_metadata_v1`.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nAITER is included in the existing registered FP8 DSA decode matrix.\n\nOn MI355X TP4 with `amd/GLM-5.2-MXFP4`, FP8 KV cache, AITER DSA prefill/decode,\nand CUDA graphs through decode batch 64, the parent revision faulted in\n`aiter::mla_a16w8_qh16_m16x4_n16x1_coex0_mask1_ps`. The corrected path\ncompleted 60k-input/600-output eager execution and CUDA graph capture/replay\nwithout the fault. Eager and graph-enabled runs produced identical output.\n\nThe serving reproduction used 60,000 input tokens, 600 output tokens,\nconcurrency 4, 32 prompts, and seed 15.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nThis is a correctness fix. No standalone serving-speed improvement is claimed;\ndecode metadata reuse is submitted separately.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nLaunch the parent or candidate revision on MI355X:\n\n```bash\nSGLANG_USE_AITER=1 python3 -m sglang.launch_server \\\n  --model amd/GLM-5.2-MXFP4 \\\n  --tp 4 \\\n  --trust-remote-code \\\n  --attention-backend dsa \\\n  --dsa-prefill-backend aiter \\\n  --dsa-decode-backend aiter \\\n  --dsa-topk-backend sgl-kernel \\\n  --kv-cache-dtype fp8_e4m3 \\\n  --page-size 64 \\\n  --cuda-graph-max-bs-decode 64 \\\n  --disable-radix-cache \\\n  --chunked-prefill-size 32768 \\\n  --max-prefill-tokens 32768\n```\n\nRun 60,000 input tokens and 600 output tokens at concurrency 4 with 32 prompts\nand seed 15. The parent revision faults during eager execution or CUDA graph\ncapture/replay; the candidate completes the workload.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format and code-style checks pass.\n- [x] Reuse the registered FP8 decode matrix for AITER coverage.\n- [ ] Run the registered matrix on the exact rebased head.\n- [x] Run exact-head MI355X eager and CUDA graph validation.\n- [x] No user-facing documentation change is required.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37754553277](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37754553277)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37754552827](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37754552827)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37754553210](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37754553210)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
